  "body": "## What changed\n\nA work offset whose placement is non-finite (NaN or infinite origin or rotation, or a zero-norm rotation quaternion) used to slip past the rotated-offset post refusal: its measured angle came out as 0, so it posted as unrotated. Such an offset is now refused by name at every entry point:\n\n- **Post check** (`posting_wcs_rotation.rs`): a new `offset_frame(&Location)` sorts a placement into `Square` / `Rotated` / `NonFinite`. A `NonFinite` offset gets its own refusal: `work offset G54 has a non-finite placement (origin or rotation) - re-place the offset before posting (operations: ...)`.\n- **`SetWcsOrigin`**: it already refused these values; its messages now name the slot (`work offset G55: rotation must be finite ...`).\n- **Project load** (`project/validate.rs`): a WCS row with a non-finite translation or rotation, or an all-zero rotation, is refused as corrupt by name. Before, the loader quietly turned an all-zero rotation into the identity.\n- **3-2-1 align**: no change needed. It refuses a non-finite frame already and writes through `SetWcsOrigin`.\n- **Setup sheet**: a rotated offset now gets a line under its translation, `rotated 90.000 deg about Z - the post refuses a rotated offset`. A non-finite one says so too. Unrotated offsets print exactly as before.\n\nDecisions are recorded in `docs/decisions/327-nonfinite-wcs-rotation.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- A NaN rotation can't reach the world through the normal paths: the command refuses it, and `model::set_transform` replaces it with the identity. So the post-check refusal is a backstop, and its tests write the bad value onto the offset entity directly.\n- JSON can't encode NaN or infinity, so the load test covers the all-zero rotation.\n- Overlap with draft PR #331: it edits one line of `posting_wcs_rotation.rs` (the `wcs_slot(...)` call) next to lines this PR changes, and the \"program offset\" lines of `render_wcs`, which this PR leaves alone. Expect a small merge in `posting_wcs_rotation.rs`.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/rotated_wcs.rs`)\n\n- `set_wcs_origin_refuses_a_non_finite_placement_by_slot`\n- `a_non_finite_offset_rotation_is_refused_by_the_post_gate`\n- `a_non_finite_offset_origin_is_refused_by_the_post_gate`\n- `project_load_refuses_a_degenerate_offset_rotation`\n- `the_setup_sheet_states_the_offset_rotation`\n\nGate: `scripts/gate.sh quick` (macOS): every app suite passes. One run of `project_roundtrip` aborted (SIGABRT) while three gates shared the machine; it was then 30/30 green run alone, and this diff does not touch that suite (noted as a possible pre-existing flake). clippy `-p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` is clean. Suites run: rotated_wcs, setup_sheet, setup_wcs, project_roundtrip, wcs_align, posting, commands_undo, setups, face_origin, app lib.\n\nChangelog: A work offset with a non-finite or zero-length rotation, or a non-finite origin, is refused by name when set, on project load and at post, instead of posting as unrotated; the setup sheet states an offset's rotation (#327)\n\nFixes #327\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
